The 5th Commandment:


Thou shalt not kill!


Just beat your breast, oh man, and praise loudly that you are not a murderer! For killing is murder, and according to your conviction you have never transgressed the Lord's commandment. You can stand before him proudly and look forward to opening this very page of your book of life with hope, without fear or anxiety.


But have you ever considered that for you there is also a he kill and that he kill is synonymous with killing?


There is no difference in that. You only make it in your way of expressing yourself, in your language; because the commandment does not say one-sidedly: You shall not kill any material life on earth! But broadly, comprehensively, in short: You shall not kill!


For example, a father had a son. The father was driven by a small earthly ambition that his son should study at any cost. But this son had gifts that urged him to do other things, and studying was of no use to him.


It was quite natural that the son had no desire for this forced study, nor was he able to muster the strength to do it. But the father demanded obedience. The son obeyed. He strove to do his father's will at the expense of his health. But since it was against the son's nature, against the gifts he had, it was quite natural that his body would also suffer.


I will not pursue this case any further, as it is so often repeated in earthly life. But it is irrefutable that the father tried to kill something in this son through his ambition or stubbornness that the son had been given to earth to develop! In many cases it is actually possible to kill it, since development is hardly possible in later life because the healthy main force for it was broken in the best of times and carelessly wasted on things that are alien to the boy's nature.


The father thereby seriously violated the commandment: Thou shalt not kill! Quite apart from the fact that by his actions he was withholding something from people that could perhaps be of great benefit to them through the boy! However, he must remember that the boy is or could be spiritually related to him or his mother, but that he nevertheless remains a separate personality before the Creator, which is obliged to develop the gifts that he was given on earth for his own good.


Perhaps, through God's grace, the boy was even granted the opportunity to redeem a heavy karma by inventing something that would, in some sense, be of great benefit to humanity!


This guilt of preventing something from happening falls especially heavily on the father or mother who placed their small worldviews above the great threads of fate and thus abused their power of parenthood.


It is no different when parents are capable of allowing the petty calculations of their minds to dominate their children's marriages. How often is the noblest feeling of their child ruthlessly stifled, thereby giving the child not only earthly carelessness, but also spiritual unhappiness, which has a more profound effect on the child's existence than all money and earthly possessions.


Of course, parents should not give in to every dream or wish of a child. That would not be fulfilling their parental duty. But serious examination is required, which must never be earthly and one-sided! But it is precisely this selfless examination that is rarely or never used by parents.


There are thousands of cases like this. There is no need for me to talk about it any more. Think about it yourself so that you do not violate this very serious word of God in the commandment! Unimagined paths will open up for you!


But the child can also stifle the parents' hopes, which are justified! If the child does not develop the gifts within itself, as is necessary in order to achieve great things, as soon as the parents have accommodatingly let the child choose the path that it has asked for. Then too the noble feelings of the parents are killed, and the commandment has been violated in a crude manner!


Even if a person somehow deceives true friendship or trust that someone has given him. He kills and thereby injures something in the other that really contains life! It is a violation of God's word: Thou shalt not kill! It brings him a bad fate that he must resolve.


You see that all commandments are only the best friends for people, to protect them from evil and suffering! Therefore, love them and respect them as a treasure, which only brings you joy in guarding!


